  <h2>Discount Codes</h2>
  <div class="content-box content-box--tan">
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Instabridge:</strong> SP20, {{ instaBest.discount | lower }}. Enter it on the web store, not in the app. <a href="/instabridge/">Full code list &rarr;</a></li>
      <li><strong>Nomad:</strong> TRAVELESIMEXPERT, {{ nomadBest.discount | lower }}. <a href="/nomad/">Full code list &rarr;</a></li>
    </ul>
    <p class="content-note">Neither code is ours. These are public codes. We confirmed SP20 at Instabridge checkout, but Nomad's homepage banner no longer shows its codes, so check that the discount appears before you pay.</p>
  </div>

  <h2>Is Instabridge or Nomad the Right Pick</h2>
  <div class="decision-grid">
    <div class="decision-card decision-card--primary">
      <h3>Go with Instabridge if&hellip;</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>You're headed somewhere with plenty of community-mapped hotspots and want data only as a backup</li>
        <li>You want a small plan, like 1GB or 3GB, at a low price</li>
        <li>You're happy buying on the web store so the 20% code applies</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="decision-card decision-card--secondary">
      <h3>Go with Nomad if&hellip;</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>You want to test the service first with the free 1GB trial eSIM</li>
        <li>You'll be away for months and want a bundle valid for up to a year</li>
        <li>You want 24/7 live chat and hotspot sharing off your phone's data</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2>Two Things Worth Knowing Before You Decide</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>A hotspot database is only as good as its community.</strong> It's strongest in busy, well-travelled cities and weaker in rural areas, so if you're heading off the beaten path, Nomad's eSIM doesn't depend on other travelers having been there first.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Neither is the cheapest for a data-heavy trip.</strong> <a href="/airhub/">Airhub</a> usually runs cheaper per gigabyte. If you want unlimited data instead of a GB bucket, see <a href="/holafly/">Holafly</a>. For device setup, see our <a href="/compatible-devices/">eSIM compatible devices</a> guide.
  </p>

  <h2>Instabridge vs Nomad FAQ</h2>
  <div class="content-faq">
    <div class="content-faq-item">
      <h3>Which is cheaper, Instabridge or Nomad</h3>
      <p>For small plans, Instabridge: its US 1GB for 7 days is $2 and 10GB for 30 days is $12. Nomad's value is in its year-long Global-EX bundles rather than cheap small plans. Prices change, so confirm at checkout.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="content-faq-item">
      <h3>Can I enter an Instabridge code in the app</h3>
      <p>No. Instabridge's support told us promo codes only work at checkout on its web store, store.instabridge.com/mobile-data.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="content-faq-item">
      <h3>Can I try either one for free</h3>
      <p>Nomad offers new customers a free 1GB trial eSIM. Instabridge's WiFi map is free to use, but we haven't seen a free eSIM from it.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="content-faq-item">
      <h3>Which is better for months abroad</h3>
      <p>Nomad. Its Global-EX bundles of 10GB to 50GB stay valid for up to a year, while Instabridge's plans we checked run 7 to 30 days.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

